INFO:__main__:ID 9 Answer: The conversation shows Katrine bringing flowers and discussing arrangements with others. She mentions "we" when referring to distributing flowers, indicating group involvement. From earlier dialogue, she says “the six of us” will handle different tasks including arranging flowers. This suggests collaboration among several individuals mentioned—Shure, Lucy, and possibly Tasha—but only specific names appear consistently across actions related to handling flowers. Based solely on who participated actively during setup/arrangement phases involving cutting/scissors/vases/bouquets:

Alice asked where scissors were; Shure suggested showcasing items initially but didn’t help physically later; Katrina led efforts throughout regarding purchasing & organizing flowers while mentioning distribution roles (“each gets one”). However no direct mention exists between any other person helping specifically *unpack* except through shared effort implied via collective action ("everyone") — yet none explicitly assist beyond general participation unless named otherwise.

But crucial detail lies within sequence showing actual physical interaction post-opening boxes – particularly focusing upon those involved near vase placement + arrangement steps which include **me**, since speaker uses personal pronouns such as 'i' repeatedly describing movements toward objects/stools etc., implying active role alongside katrinas instructions being followed closely per narrative flow suggesting joint activity under leadership direction without naming additional helpers besides self-reference point ('Me') plus possible indirect assistance inferred indirectly due lack clarity outside stated participants listed above...

